  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreCare 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your mother\u2019s treatment plan requires her to take medications at
    exact times each day. You share that this complex dosing schedule combined with
    the side effects from treatment have made it hard for her to stay on track without
    constant help.\n\n<b>Based on this scenario, how might caregiver feedback influence
    preclinical research?</b>"
  explanation: When caregivers share how hard it can be to manage complex medication
    schedules and side effects at home, researchers can take this into account early
    on, guiding them toward treatment options that may be easier to follow and fit
    better into everyday life. By considering these challenges during preclinical
    research, scientists can focus on treatments that are not only effective but
    also more realistic for patients and families to manage.
  correctAnswer: It can guide researchers toward treatment options that are more
    manageable for patients and caregivers in everyday life.
  incorrectAnswer1: It helps researchers better understand the emotional bond between
    caregivers and patients during treatment.
  incorrectAnswer2: It gives caregivers permission to change how medications are
    prescribed during clinical care.
  incorrectAnswer3: None of these answers
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
